        "description": "The tap-specific machinery picture (req-git-serious-double-tap-tap-projection): a double-tap-owned projection whose one elevation runs TWO layouts on the same canvas — git_serious's machinery layout (github_core's machinery.js, referenced by entity id, never copied) and then the tap lanes layout (this plugin's tap-machinery.js), which regroups the repository's workflows into lanes by what starts them (PR gate · publish · scheduled · fleet · reusable baseline), places them by the cardinal map ruled 2026-09-09 (gate centre, publish left, scheduled below, fleet and baseline at the bottom, sources right), and draws the workflow-call and workflow_run edges across lanes. One graph panel owns the projection and shares the generic repository page's three scene searches by id; the tap page mounts it with the fixed input repo=unified-systems-com/tap. Out-of-file endpoints: git_serious's layout and searches, so git_serious seeds first."
